{"author":{"id":"7674679dac9170669f752d932f8b5955b1d55717359e13b1c1e687003c7bb99f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792096991,"nonce":"AARNh9JuDeSBCs4NOsMz274TG9Q=","title":"git-work as an app: a palette, a finder, a home, and search","message":"Design: doc/design/app.md, proposed 2026-10-15, not approved.\n\nToday a flow is the only way onto a page: an issue the flow did not plan for opens bare, there is no search, most commands are letters only `?` lists, and pickers narrow only after `/`. This story makes the terminal an application: one keymap, an esc palette, a typable finder, a per-type default show, `git work` opening a home flow, and search over descriptions.\n\nTakes in doc/design/link-fields.md (proposed), revised to fit: L4 becomes the default `links` expand, L5 edits on space and offers inverses.","files":null,"fields":{"area":["tui"],"priority":"high","status":"backlog","type":"story"}}]}